1
00:00:00,014 --> 00:00:01,525
(This drama complied with production
guidelines for filming child actors,)

2
00:00:01,527 --> 00:00:03,000
(and some scenes used
generative AI technology.)

3
00:00:03,100 --> 00:00:05,160
(Episode 58)

4
00:00:13,865 --> 00:00:15,859
Did something bad happen to Seung Hyun?

5
00:00:16,521 --> 00:00:18,985
What's wrong? Want some kimchi?

6
00:00:19,061 --> 00:00:20,061
No, it's okay.

7
00:00:24,077 --> 00:00:25,077
Today...

8
00:00:25,373 --> 00:00:27,100
was Seung Hyun's birthday.

9
00:00:27,772 --> 00:00:29,990
I was so caught up in my own life
that I didn't know it was his birthday,

10
00:00:30,232 --> 00:00:32,512
and I don't even know
what he's going through.

11
00:00:33,318 --> 00:00:35,915
Su Yeon, can I even call myself a mom?

12
00:00:36,241 --> 00:00:37,241
Yeong Ju.

13
00:00:39,371 --> 00:00:41,348
Soju too?

14
00:00:42,132 --> 00:00:44,505
I'm sorry about earlier.
Something urgent came up all of a sudden.

15
00:00:44,972 --> 00:00:46,932
- Did you finish all the kimchi?
- Yeah.

16
00:00:47,232 --> 00:00:48,970
The two of us did it all day.

17
00:00:49,156 --> 00:00:50,512
I'll help next time.

18
00:00:51,258 --> 00:00:54,252
Why did your oldest son go
to the police station?

19
00:00:54,489 --> 00:00:55,947
I heard he quit his government job.

20
00:00:57,501 --> 00:01:00,350
Since she asked...

21
00:01:01,183 --> 00:01:03,329
It's okay.
You don't have to worry about him.

22
00:01:03,354 --> 00:01:06,728
How can I not worry? He's family.

23
00:01:07,406 --> 00:01:09,736
I heard he's driving a truck around
selling things.

24
00:01:10,512 --> 00:01:13,212
If he's having such a hard time,
you should've said something.

25
00:01:13,237 --> 00:01:14,883
What's the point of having friends
if you can't help each other?

26
00:01:15,389 --> 00:01:16,673
I can even lend you some money.

27
00:01:16,698 --> 00:01:18,258
There's no need for that.

28
00:01:18,432 --> 00:01:20,140
He's not doing it because he needs money.

29
00:01:20,165 --> 00:01:21,719
Why are you getting angry?

30
00:01:23,052 --> 00:01:26,022
I heard your grandson died
and your daughter-in-law left too.

31
00:01:26,832 --> 00:01:28,253
There's no need to look at her.

32
00:01:28,479 --> 00:01:29,926
I asked her because I was curious.

33
00:01:30,215 --> 00:01:31,703
I need to know what's going on
so I can help.

34
00:01:31,728 --> 00:01:33,511
I told you, we don't need any help.

35
00:01:33,646 --> 00:01:35,124
We don't, Sun Kyung.

36
00:01:35,412 --> 00:01:39,259
When he came to our house,
your oldest son looked so good.

37
00:01:40,034 --> 00:01:41,815
Is he out of his mind?

38
00:01:41,865 --> 00:01:44,446
If I were in his shoes,
I think I'd have gone crazy.

39
00:01:44,800 --> 00:01:46,742
He must've been heartbroken.

40
00:01:46,767 --> 00:01:49,033
Hey, you really need to be good to him.

41
00:01:49,058 --> 00:01:50,633
What do you mean, out of his mind?

42
00:01:50,872 --> 00:01:52,948
Don't talk about him like that.
He's perfectly fine.

43
00:01:52,972 --> 00:01:54,194
How am I talking about him like that?

44
00:01:54,219 --> 00:01:55,640
Can't I be concerned about him?

45
00:01:56,081 --> 00:01:57,188
Come on...

46
00:01:57,213 --> 00:02:00,817
Why do you only hear part of what I say?
Listen to the whole thing.

47
00:02:01,858 --> 00:02:04,578
- Do you have an inferiority complex?
- Enough!

48
00:02:05,052 --> 00:02:06,413
You think I don't know you?

49
00:02:06,552 --> 00:02:09,003
You're pretending to worry about him
while actually looking down on him. Right?

50
00:02:09,028 --> 00:02:10,421
For goodness' sake...

51
00:02:10,685 --> 00:02:12,018
Su Yeon, am I really like that?

52
00:02:12,428 --> 00:02:13,684
No.

53
00:02:13,701 --> 00:02:15,718
She's saying that
because she's worried, Yeong Ju.

54
00:02:16,159 --> 00:02:18,420
I mean, younger madam. What's wrong?

55
00:02:18,421 --> 00:02:20,320
Enough!

56
00:02:21,831 --> 00:02:23,119
What's all the noise about?

57
00:02:24,392 --> 00:02:27,433
Yeong Ju's drunk and making a scene.

58
00:02:27,798 --> 00:02:30,364
Yeong Ju, sober up
and get a hold of yourself.

59
00:02:54,785 --> 00:02:58,362
You put up with a friend who's drunk.
That's what friends do.

60
00:02:58,512 --> 00:02:59,910
You were being cold
to her again, weren't you?

61
00:03:00,384 --> 00:03:02,011
What do you take me for?

62
00:03:02,057 --> 00:03:03,517
Yeong Ju's oldest son,

63
00:03:03,639 --> 00:03:08,059
who was a government employee,
beat a guy up and ended up at the station.

64
00:03:08,084 --> 00:03:11,105
- How was I supposed to comfort her?
- Really?

65
00:03:11,412 --> 00:03:12,852
There must be a reason.

66
00:03:12,877 --> 00:03:15,386
His son died, his wife left,

67
00:03:15,410 --> 00:03:17,201
and he even quit his government job.

68
00:03:17,685 --> 00:03:20,027
That's why I asked
if he was out of his mind.

69
00:03:20,052 --> 00:03:21,232
Think about it.

70
00:03:21,679 --> 00:03:23,559
Wouldn't it be stranger
if he were perfectly normal?

71
00:03:23,560 --> 00:03:26,267
Come on. Who says something like that?

72
00:03:26,292 --> 00:03:29,291
You were in the wrong. Even if you know,
you should pretend you don't.

73
00:03:29,704 --> 00:03:31,890
She was drinking soju alone,
and you still had to lecture her?

74
00:03:32,110 --> 00:03:34,387
Why don't you take my side anymore?

75
00:03:35,038 --> 00:03:37,001
I brought it up
because I wanted to comfort her.

76
00:03:37,152 --> 00:03:39,947
How can you comfort someone
by pretending you don't know? Am I wrong?

77
00:03:39,972 --> 00:03:42,818
You wait until she brings it up herself,
then you talk about it gently.

78
00:03:44,764 --> 00:03:45,821
Honey,

79
00:03:46,351 --> 00:03:50,342
who was the woman you were with
at the hotel cafe the other day?

80
00:03:50,832 --> 00:03:51,912
Why are you suddenly asking about that?

81
00:03:51,937 --> 00:03:53,890
My friend said you looked so happy.

82
00:03:54,432 --> 00:03:56,256
She asked me if you were having an affair.

83
00:03:56,281 --> 00:03:58,226
What nonsense are you talking about?

84
00:03:58,251 --> 00:04:00,299
You scared me. Why are you yelling?

85
00:04:00,324 --> 00:04:01,574
Do you really think I'm that kind of man?

86
00:04:01,599 --> 00:04:03,272
Is that all you think of me?

87
00:04:08,424 --> 00:04:09,950
Never mind, then. Why...

88
00:04:10,089 --> 00:04:11,210
What's with him?

89
00:04:24,987 --> 00:04:26,427
Look somewhere else, will you?

90
00:04:26,452 --> 00:04:28,380
How am I supposed to eat
with you staring at me?

91
00:04:28,692 --> 00:04:31,342
There are wine bottles all over the house.

92
00:04:31,664 --> 00:04:33,352
- I'm throwing them all out.
- No.

93
00:04:34,372 --> 00:04:36,827
Why on earth can't you sleep?

94
00:04:37,254 --> 00:04:38,486
What are you worried about?

95
00:04:39,204 --> 00:04:40,765
That you won't be able to get married.

96
00:04:40,790 --> 00:04:43,503
This whole marriage thing!

97
00:04:55,652 --> 00:04:57,173
That hits the spot.

98
00:05:01,957 --> 00:05:04,534
Are you the baby's mom
from the motorcycle accident?

99
00:05:04,680 --> 00:05:06,635
I was wondering
if it was Pumseongak's motorcycle.

100
00:05:28,892 --> 00:05:31,602
Once we wrap up this book fair,
things should finally calm down a little.

101
00:05:32,184 --> 00:05:35,053
The weather's getting cooler too,

102
00:05:35,077 --> 00:05:37,648
so it'd be nice
if we could take a few days off.

103
00:05:38,292 --> 00:05:40,993
I'll discuss it with the CEO
once we wrap up the book fair.

104
00:05:41,772 --> 00:05:43,341
It's not exactly a startup,

105
00:05:43,440 --> 00:05:45,545
but we haven't had any time off
since we started this new venture.

106
00:05:47,744 --> 00:05:49,655
If we never switch off,
we can't really switch on.

107
00:05:49,905 --> 00:05:50,908
I've been thinking about it.

108
00:05:52,752 --> 00:05:54,874
But have you seen this?

109
00:05:55,785 --> 00:05:58,466
Do Do Hee of Love in Zip staged a hoax
to get attention,

110
00:05:58,490 --> 00:06:00,946
and falsely accused her ex
of leaving her for someone else.

111
00:06:00,971 --> 00:06:02,987
Looks like Do Do Hee's really getting hit
with some serious backlash.

112
00:06:03,012 --> 00:06:04,217
She's basically public enemy...

113
00:06:05,471 --> 00:06:08,241
She's getting absolutely roasted.

114
00:06:22,932 --> 00:06:24,315
Your birthday's tomorrow.
Do you have plans?

115
00:06:25,465 --> 00:06:27,957
Are you going to hang out
with Jung A and Tae O again?

116
00:06:28,677 --> 00:06:30,379
How did you know it's my birthday?

117
00:06:30,403 --> 00:06:31,765
We signed an employment contract.

118
00:06:33,091 --> 00:06:36,552
Actually, Jung A keeps telling me
to look forward to it.

119
00:06:37,512 --> 00:06:39,565
I wish you'd invite me too.

120
00:06:42,518 --> 00:06:44,832
By the way, are you free tonight?

121
00:06:45,925 --> 00:06:48,809
Professor Bae has a private exhibition.

122
00:06:49,070 --> 00:06:51,652
Really? Not just anyone gets invited.

123
00:06:54,045 --> 00:06:57,266
We're not in the same league
just because we work at the same place.

124
00:06:57,291 --> 00:06:58,926
It's business, after all.

125
00:06:59,609 --> 00:07:01,867
Want to come with me?
I have a plus-one ticket.

126
00:07:02,952 --> 00:07:04,327
I'd love to.

127
00:07:04,352 --> 00:07:05,894
It's been a long time
since I've seen Professor Bae.

128
00:07:06,458 --> 00:07:08,121
We said we wouldn't worry
about what other people think.

129
00:07:08,535 --> 00:07:09,535
Let's go together.

130
00:07:11,301 --> 00:07:13,037
Okay. I'll go.

131
00:07:32,605 --> 00:07:34,611
This is killing me.

132
00:07:37,167 --> 00:07:39,163
(Cha Seung Woo)

133
00:07:40,531 --> 00:07:43,719
The person you are calling is unavailable.
Please leave a message...

134
00:07:45,247 --> 00:07:46,418
I wonder if she's okay.

135
00:07:47,676 --> 00:07:48,856
Seriously...

136
00:07:49,185 --> 00:07:50,973
She really has me worried.

137
00:07:52,125 --> 00:07:53,663
Go check on her at home.

138
00:07:53,951 --> 00:07:56,453
Some cyber bullies may have found her...

139
00:07:56,455 --> 00:07:58,002
and started harassing her.

140
00:07:58,027 --> 00:07:59,839
She would've called the police.

141
00:08:00,538 --> 00:08:01,807
I'll go check on her, just in case.

142
00:08:04,218 --> 00:08:05,218
Go ahead.

143
00:08:15,091 --> 00:08:16,316
Do Hee, you in there?

144
00:08:16,838 --> 00:08:18,222
If you are, open the door.

145
00:08:21,151 --> 00:08:22,215
Do Hee!

146
00:08:38,478 --> 00:08:39,605
What?

147
00:08:52,029 --> 00:08:54,323
Close the door.

148
00:08:54,488 --> 00:08:56,230
Take a shower. You stink.

149
00:09:19,272 --> 00:09:21,543
If you're such a coward,
why would you tell a lie like that?

150
00:09:23,327 --> 00:09:24,740
It wasn't a lie.

151
00:09:25,678 --> 00:09:28,502
Na Ji Ni and Ji Hu put on this whole act
to make me look like this.

152
00:09:29,352 --> 00:09:31,085
They're going to end up dating anyway.

153
00:09:32,232 --> 00:09:35,507
Whether they date or not,
you need to live your own life.

154
00:09:35,972 --> 00:09:37,768
I used to obsess over my past too,

155
00:09:39,183 --> 00:09:41,047
but it doesn't do you any good.
Don't do it.

156
00:09:41,049 --> 00:09:43,293
I don't want to!

157
00:09:43,318 --> 00:09:44,908
I'm going to see them fall apart.

158
00:09:44,933 --> 00:09:46,083
I'm the only one suffering.

159
00:09:46,898 --> 00:09:49,660
For once, my parents were proud of me,
and then I got scolded again.

160
00:09:50,305 --> 00:09:52,046
Meanwhile, they're living it up.

161
00:09:52,345 --> 00:09:54,510
I can't let that happen!

162
00:09:54,535 --> 00:09:56,707
You're living well too!

163
00:09:59,719 --> 00:10:02,994
At your age, why do you still care so much
about your parents' approval?

164
00:10:03,432 --> 00:10:05,490
You have a nice house
and plenty of followers,

165
00:10:07,291 --> 00:10:08,430
so forget Na Ji Ni.

166
00:10:09,012 --> 00:10:10,215
You said her blood was dirty.

167
00:10:10,512 --> 00:10:12,227
How do you know Na Ji Ni's blood is dirty?

168
00:10:12,252 --> 00:10:13,724
You said it yourself.

169
00:10:15,261 --> 00:10:16,261
Enough.

170
00:10:16,672 --> 00:10:18,233
This is so frustrating.

171
00:10:18,732 --> 00:10:21,024
Nobody knows...

172
00:10:22,298 --> 00:10:24,495
how she ruined my school years.

173
00:10:24,672 --> 00:10:26,233
Wasn't Na Ji Ni the one who suffered?

174
00:10:27,671 --> 00:10:28,671
Director.

175
00:10:29,531 --> 00:10:31,047
What is Na Ji Ni to you?

176
00:10:31,972 --> 00:10:34,589
Nothing. I just know her a little.

177
00:10:34,911 --> 00:10:36,319
Director, you're on my side, right?

178
00:10:37,305 --> 00:10:40,014
That's why you came, right?
You were worried about me.

179
00:10:40,922 --> 00:10:41,922
Go to sleep.

180
00:10:42,278 --> 00:10:44,161
Get some sleep and forget everything.

181
00:10:44,772 --> 00:10:47,814
Well, you don't have to forget.
You can think about it,

182
00:10:48,807 --> 00:10:50,424
but think of your own life first.

183
00:10:51,732 --> 00:10:53,281
People will laugh at you.

184
00:10:53,938 --> 00:10:55,215
You live in such a nice house,

185
00:10:55,587 --> 00:10:57,722
enjoying all this
without ever working part-time.

186
00:10:58,343 --> 00:11:00,877
- You'll pay for being ungrateful.
- Stop yelling.

187
00:11:00,902 --> 00:11:02,069
My head hurts.

188
00:11:07,685 --> 00:11:08,823
Don't go.

189
00:11:09,538 --> 00:11:11,507
Stay with me until I fall asleep.

190
00:11:12,385 --> 00:11:14,303
I feel lonely.

191
00:11:16,425 --> 00:11:17,425
Do Hee,

192
00:11:18,201 --> 00:11:19,578
I'm not here to babysit you.

193
00:11:29,244 --> 00:11:30,365
Sober up...

194
00:11:31,027 --> 00:11:32,607
and come to your senses, please.

195
00:11:36,545 --> 00:11:37,702
Director...

196
00:11:38,367 --> 00:11:39,635
I feel so down.

197
00:11:40,771 --> 00:11:41,910
My mom,

198
00:11:42,390 --> 00:11:43,472
my dad,

199
00:11:43,848 --> 00:11:44,932
and Ji Hu.

200
00:11:47,111 --> 00:11:48,653
They're all so unfair to me.

201
00:12:04,891 --> 00:12:06,858
Okay, good. That was a nice turn.

202
00:12:06,883 --> 00:12:07,883
Okay, one more time.

203
00:12:08,096 --> 00:12:10,942
Good. That's great.

204
00:12:10,967 --> 00:12:12,506
Okay, good. Last one.

205
00:12:14,811 --> 00:12:17,334
That was great. Let's take a short break.

206
00:12:17,358 --> 00:12:19,012
Okay, good work, everyone.

207
00:12:22,684 --> 00:12:23,848
You looked so beautiful.

208
00:12:28,811 --> 00:12:29,844
Right.

209
00:12:30,973 --> 00:12:32,310
Wait a second, please.

210
00:12:36,452 --> 00:12:37,634
Excuse me...

211
00:12:39,731 --> 00:12:41,559
What brings you here?

212
00:12:41,577 --> 00:12:43,380
I know a director here.

213
00:12:43,692 --> 00:12:45,407
We were discussing a brand investment,

214
00:12:45,431 --> 00:12:47,054
and they invited me to see the set.

215
00:12:47,935 --> 00:12:50,113
So you're a model here, Se Ri?

216
00:12:50,114 --> 00:12:52,007
Well, I'm not the main model.

217
00:12:52,032 --> 00:12:54,660
These photos are for the website.

218
00:12:55,055 --> 00:12:57,602
The main model seems to be done.
You should've come earlier.

219
00:12:57,603 --> 00:12:59,027
That's okay.

220
00:12:59,052 --> 00:13:01,222
I'd rather see you, Se Ri.

221
00:13:01,246 --> 00:13:02,579
Thank you.

222
00:13:02,892 --> 00:13:05,722
Joong Bin, you're more impressive
than I thought.

223
00:13:05,746 --> 00:13:07,127
Not really.

224
00:13:07,623 --> 00:13:09,743
We were in the Navy together.

225
00:13:11,155 --> 00:13:13,115
He's an outside director here,
so I came by.

226
00:13:13,244 --> 00:13:15,416
- I see.
- Se Ri, you have a call.

227
00:13:15,863 --> 00:13:17,442
Excuse me.

228
00:13:19,365 --> 00:13:20,622
Hey, what's up?

229
00:13:21,798 --> 00:13:24,646
How did you know
it was my daughter's birthday?

230
00:13:24,704 --> 00:13:27,087
I got her a gift. Let's meet up.

231
00:13:27,459 --> 00:13:29,133
Okay. I'll come as soon as I'm done.

232
00:13:30,258 --> 00:13:32,115
So it's your daughter's birthday.

233
00:13:32,139 --> 00:13:33,139
Yes.

234
00:13:33,699 --> 00:13:35,328
She's someone I wasn't close to before.

235
00:13:35,752 --> 00:13:38,459
She's buying my daughter a birthday gift,

236
00:13:38,483 --> 00:13:40,154
so I'm really touched.

237
00:13:41,025 --> 00:13:43,304
Life is long. There's plenty to live for.

238
00:13:43,508 --> 00:13:45,690
I find it boring because it's so long.

239
00:13:46,156 --> 00:13:48,271
Just wait. It'll get more exciting.

240
00:13:48,273 --> 00:13:50,435
Even fun gets boring if it never stops.

241
00:13:50,459 --> 00:13:52,770
You have a point. I'll remember that.

242
00:13:53,307 --> 00:13:54,717
I think the break is over.

243
00:13:55,124 --> 00:13:57,240
I'll let you get back to work.
I'll head out.

244
00:13:57,265 --> 00:13:58,824
Okay.

245
00:14:01,487 --> 00:14:04,255
Who was that?
He said he's close to a director here.

246
00:14:04,401 --> 00:14:08,008
I knew him when I worked part-time.
I didn't expect to see him here.

247
00:14:09,736 --> 00:14:11,497
Here's the next concept. Take a look.

248
00:14:19,366 --> 00:14:21,366
(ShoeallS)

249
00:14:26,175 --> 00:14:27,247
So many styles.

250
00:14:27,732 --> 00:14:29,215
Right.

251
00:14:35,571 --> 00:14:37,314
These are the ones you wear, right?

252
00:14:39,642 --> 00:14:40,642
How about these?

253
00:14:41,537 --> 00:14:43,296
Why? Are they for Yeong Ju?

254
00:14:43,298 --> 00:14:46,056
No, I want to get a pair each
for Lieutenant No and Su Yeon.

255
00:14:46,058 --> 00:14:48,378
You wear yours so much,
so I trust they're good.

256
00:14:50,145 --> 00:14:51,418
Then how about these?

257
00:14:52,831 --> 00:14:55,255
I did some research
after you bought me mine.

258
00:14:55,256 --> 00:14:57,659
Since Lieutenant No walks a lot,

259
00:14:58,232 --> 00:14:59,879
these shoe soles are special,

260
00:15:00,164 --> 00:15:03,072
so your feet stay comfortable
when you stand or walk for a long time.

261
00:15:03,252 --> 00:15:05,104
When did you become such an expert?

262
00:15:06,252 --> 00:15:08,258
Do you really want to run a store?

263
00:15:08,538 --> 00:15:11,183
My mom always said
I should earn money myself.

264
00:15:11,185 --> 00:15:12,885
She kept saying it over and over.

265
00:15:13,766 --> 00:15:14,766
Should I try it?

266
00:15:19,495 --> 00:15:20,672
- Excuse me.
- Yes?

267
00:15:20,892 --> 00:15:23,935
I started wearing them
after my husband gave me a pair.

268
00:15:24,049 --> 00:15:26,091
Now I can't stand wearing heels.

269
00:15:26,698 --> 00:15:29,998
They're stylish and so comfortable,

270
00:15:31,871 --> 00:15:33,375
so they're all I wear these days.

271
00:15:33,512 --> 00:15:34,525
- Really?
- Yes.

272
00:15:34,752 --> 00:15:35,752
Try them on.

273
00:15:40,868 --> 00:15:43,458
You seemed really happy
chatting with customers.

274
00:15:43,652 --> 00:15:45,587
I think you'd be good at it. Try it.

275
00:15:46,320 --> 00:15:47,320
You think so?

276
00:15:58,938 --> 00:16:01,445
You come here a lot, handsome young man.

277
00:16:01,738 --> 00:16:02,964
You run a restaurant, right?

278
00:16:03,365 --> 00:16:04,365
A food truck.

279
00:16:04,592 --> 00:16:05,948
And I'm a dad.

280
00:16:06,455 --> 00:16:07,455
Really?

281
00:16:08,218 --> 00:16:10,598
I can't tell people's ages these days.

282
00:16:11,305 --> 00:16:12,805
You got a new hairstyle.

283
00:16:14,571 --> 00:16:17,606
I changed it a while ago.
How do you still remember?

284
00:16:17,819 --> 00:16:18,860
Thank you for noticing.

285
00:16:18,872 --> 00:16:20,199
My husband didn't even notice.

286
00:16:20,200 --> 00:16:21,691
I'm sure he noticed.

287
00:16:21,758 --> 00:16:23,005
He's just pretending he didn't.

288
00:16:23,492 --> 00:16:25,899
If he admits it, you'll ask
if it looks nice and if it suits you.

289
00:16:26,060 --> 00:16:27,447
He wants to avoid all those questions.

290
00:16:27,588 --> 00:16:28,697
Your son's the same.

291
00:16:28,992 --> 00:16:29,992
Really?

292
00:16:30,208 --> 00:16:31,394
If he says he noticed, you'll ask...

293
00:16:31,581 --> 00:16:33,097
if you look nice and if you look young.

294
00:16:33,392 --> 00:16:35,912
That's when the nonstop chatter starts.

295
00:16:36,612 --> 00:16:40,378
So men say they didn't notice
to avoid starting that conversation.

296
00:16:40,552 --> 00:16:42,398
Then you'll sigh deeply and say,

297
00:16:43,472 --> 00:16:44,677
"I shouldn't even bother."

298
00:16:44,678 --> 00:16:47,132
And you'll stop talking.

299
00:16:48,124 --> 00:16:50,644
You're fun to talk to.

300
00:16:51,998 --> 00:16:54,005
I'll ring you up.

301
00:17:10,577 --> 00:17:11,904
Three of these.

302
00:17:11,905 --> 00:17:13,917
What's the total?

303
00:17:13,919 --> 00:17:16,698
Altogether, it's 54 dollars.

304
00:17:17,818 --> 00:17:19,385
I only have 30 dollars.

305
00:17:20,805 --> 00:17:23,297
I'll leave this one.

306
00:17:23,881 --> 00:17:25,611
Take it. I'll pay for it.

307
00:17:25,698 --> 00:17:28,525
You shouldn't pay for that, young man.

308
00:17:28,658 --> 00:17:30,368
My wife is Vietnamese too.

309
00:17:30,891 --> 00:17:34,074
If she were beside me,
she'd nudge me to cover it.

310
00:17:34,875 --> 00:17:35,875
Thank you.

311
00:17:36,318 --> 00:17:37,318
Thank you.

312
00:17:37,389 --> 00:17:38,976
You're so kind.

313
00:17:38,978 --> 00:17:40,514
And you're fun to talk to.

314
00:17:40,854 --> 00:17:43,698
Come by often.
I'll give you a special discount.

315
00:17:43,919 --> 00:17:44,919
Okay.

316
00:17:45,136 --> 00:17:46,136
Here you go.

317
00:17:47,222 --> 00:17:48,791
An emotional bruise?

318
00:17:49,605 --> 00:17:51,885
It's also called
post-traumatic stress disorder.

319
00:17:51,938 --> 00:17:56,458
Seung Hyun wasn't physically injured,
but he was hurt emotionally.

320
00:17:56,858 --> 00:17:58,845
He's holding up very well right now.

321
00:17:59,638 --> 00:18:02,491
He wasn't like this before,
but now he gets angry a lot.

322
00:18:02,711 --> 00:18:04,356
And when he laughs, he laughs loudly.

323
00:18:04,358 --> 00:18:05,832
He's like a different person.

324
00:18:06,638 --> 00:18:09,157
I used all my knowledge
to prepare this medicine.

325
00:18:09,412 --> 00:18:10,951
I hope it helps.

326
00:18:11,819 --> 00:18:12,896
Sa Bin.

327
00:18:13,131 --> 00:18:16,062
I should've taken care of him sooner,
but I was busy with our wedding.

328
00:18:16,159 --> 00:18:18,425
I feel so bad I didn't look after him.

329
00:18:18,765 --> 00:18:21,147
I should've been a better mom.

330
00:18:21,970 --> 00:18:25,040
It's my fault. I took you away from him.

331
00:18:25,716 --> 00:18:28,407
Normally, I'd check his pulse in person
before preparing the medicine,

332
00:18:28,409 --> 00:18:31,156
but I didn't think he'd come here,
so I made it like this.

333
00:18:31,317 --> 00:18:32,914
Next time, let me check his pulse.

334
00:18:33,082 --> 00:18:34,104
Thank you.

335
00:18:35,505 --> 00:18:37,943
By the way, teach me how to work here.

336
00:18:37,945 --> 00:18:40,570
Let's start by learning
how to clean the cupping cups.

337
00:18:41,050 --> 00:18:42,630
Good. You're my part-timer now,

338
00:18:43,038 --> 00:18:44,412
so I'm going to put you to work.

339
00:18:51,205 --> 00:18:52,205
Give it to me.

340
00:18:54,020 --> 00:18:55,020
Thanks.

341
00:18:56,252 --> 00:18:57,930
This is why having a son is nice.

342
00:18:57,932 --> 00:18:59,732
With a daughter,
I'd have to carry it all myself.

343
00:19:06,078 --> 00:19:08,425
What does Ji Ni like?

344
00:19:09,044 --> 00:19:10,044
What?

345
00:19:10,792 --> 00:19:13,186
I upset her a little.

346
00:19:14,147 --> 00:19:16,152
Why? What happened?

347
00:19:17,185 --> 00:19:18,185
I just...

348
00:19:18,600 --> 00:19:20,203
asked why she rejects love,

349
00:19:20,258 --> 00:19:21,714
and what she could possibly lack.

350
00:19:22,355 --> 00:19:24,035
I told her to stop acting like a child.

351
00:19:24,650 --> 00:19:26,306
- I'm sorry.
- Really?

352
00:19:28,728 --> 00:19:31,400
You did the right thing.

353
00:19:31,727 --> 00:19:32,727
What?

354
00:19:33,012 --> 00:19:35,758
Why would she get upset over that?

355
00:19:36,012 --> 00:19:37,378
Don't worry about it.

356
00:19:37,525 --> 00:19:40,118
Yeah, keep telling her things like that.

357
00:19:40,358 --> 00:19:43,125
When I say it, she glares at me
like she wants to kill me.

358
00:19:43,518 --> 00:19:45,451
She does the same to me, though.

359
00:19:45,452 --> 00:19:48,018
She's your younger sister. Ignore that...

360
00:19:48,132 --> 00:19:50,952
and keep telling her
what she needs to hear.

361
00:19:51,552 --> 00:19:56,104
She grew up without siblings,
with no one older to guide her.

362
00:19:57,177 --> 00:20:00,233
Her dad and I felt guilty,

363
00:20:00,242 --> 00:20:02,798
so we were always walking on eggshells
around her.

364
00:20:03,145 --> 00:20:08,127
She couldn't even go to high school
and stopped leaving her room.

365
00:20:08,748 --> 00:20:09,748
I see.

366
00:20:10,533 --> 00:20:12,065
Anyway, thanks.

367
00:20:12,558 --> 00:20:17,225
She doesn't really like anything
except working out and listening to music.

368
00:20:36,132 --> 00:20:37,219
Pick one of these.

369
00:20:38,926 --> 00:20:39,926
What?

370
00:20:40,500 --> 00:20:41,673
Bluetooth earbuds?

371
00:20:42,314 --> 00:20:44,665
- You're buying them?
- It's Ji Ni's birthday.

372
00:20:44,667 --> 00:20:46,517
You got so mad at her,

373
00:20:46,658 --> 00:20:48,985
- and you're getting her a birthday gift?
- She gave me a gift, you know.

374
00:20:49,117 --> 00:20:50,468
And I feel bad about it too.

375
00:20:52,752 --> 00:20:54,352
Why do I get mad so easily?

376
00:20:54,617 --> 00:20:56,045
I can't stand anything anymore.

377
00:20:57,171 --> 00:21:00,258
What does she have to be upset about?
We're the ones who lost our dad.

378
00:21:00,818 --> 00:21:02,537
That's what I thought too,

379
00:21:02,898 --> 00:21:05,078
but after hearing her, I can understand.

380
00:21:05,638 --> 00:21:08,170
Would you be happy if your tuition
were paid with money your parents stole?

381
00:21:08,172 --> 00:21:10,118
That's how she feels.

382
00:21:11,472 --> 00:21:14,618
When she said that,
I wanted to ask, "What do you know?"

383
00:21:14,832 --> 00:21:17,200
Ji Ni and her mom apologized to me
several times.

384
00:21:17,201 --> 00:21:18,294
And that's supposed to be enough?

385
00:21:19,005 --> 00:21:22,652
She asked if we were still looking
for accident witnesses. I got choked up.

386
00:21:23,005 --> 00:21:25,037
Even if I told you and mom
to stop looking,

387
00:21:25,078 --> 00:21:26,451
she had no right to say that.

388
00:21:26,878 --> 00:21:28,773
Whose car was I following
when this happened?

389
00:21:28,959 --> 00:21:30,172
I'm getting worked up again.

390
00:21:30,173 --> 00:21:32,499
Stop talking and help me pick.

391
00:21:38,605 --> 00:21:40,314
I'm sorry. The car's still being repaired.

392
00:21:41,291 --> 00:21:42,493
What are you sorry for?

393
00:21:43,005 --> 00:21:44,518
I take the bus all the time.

394
00:21:45,112 --> 00:21:48,907
It must be harder for you.
You're used to driving everywhere.

395
00:21:49,008 --> 00:21:50,008
Not at all.

396
00:21:50,405 --> 00:21:51,406
What do you take me for?

397
00:21:52,960 --> 00:21:54,039
A prince?

398
00:21:55,212 --> 00:21:56,212
No.

399
00:21:56,694 --> 00:21:57,694
A princess.

400
00:22:02,005 --> 00:22:03,638
I really love Professor Bae's paintings.

401
00:22:04,678 --> 00:22:08,218
I wanted to go to college
so I could study under him.

402
00:22:11,665 --> 00:22:12,757
Want to see something?

403
00:22:15,372 --> 00:22:18,285
This is my favorite painting.

404
00:22:18,678 --> 00:22:20,131
But did you know?

405
00:22:20,385 --> 00:22:23,858
Professor Bae's paintings look
slightly different from different angles.

406
00:22:24,391 --> 00:22:25,391
Especially,

407
00:22:26,504 --> 00:22:27,910
this one and...

408
00:22:28,278 --> 00:22:29,278
Where did it go?

409
00:22:32,175 --> 00:22:33,175
This one...

410
00:22:36,496 --> 00:22:37,496
Is that us?

411
00:22:38,256 --> 00:22:39,256
Yeah.

412
00:22:40,675 --> 00:22:41,760
This is embarrassing.

413
00:22:42,598 --> 00:22:45,245
I just find myself
thinking about that day a lot.

414
00:22:46,072 --> 00:22:47,378
You drew this really well.

415
00:22:47,965 --> 00:22:49,851
Can I have it? I'd like to keep it.

416
00:22:52,305 --> 00:22:53,685
Sure. Okay.

417
00:22:59,331 --> 00:23:01,554
- Mom.
- Don't call me mom.

418
00:23:01,812 --> 00:23:04,263
I never gave birth to a fool like you.

419
00:23:04,265 --> 00:23:06,631
Mom, can't you comfort me for once?

420
00:23:07,605 --> 00:23:09,372
I'm already having a hard time.
Do you have to be like this too?

421
00:23:09,373 --> 00:23:12,406
That's why I'm telling you to do better.

422
00:23:12,911 --> 00:23:15,063
I can't even face your dad because of you.

423
00:23:16,197 --> 00:23:19,305
A nationwide fraud? Seriously?

424
00:23:21,145 --> 00:23:22,364
I can't stand...

425
00:23:22,692 --> 00:23:24,349
that Ji Ni!

426
00:23:25,292 --> 00:23:27,998
Why do you let her push you around
like you can't beat her?

427
00:23:28,572 --> 00:23:30,886
I praised you just once
for actually doing something right.

428
00:23:33,307 --> 00:23:34,427
Fine.

429
00:23:34,767 --> 00:23:37,317
Then I'll just die. Happy now?

430
00:23:37,931 --> 00:23:39,599
I'll just die and be done with it.

431
00:23:43,350 --> 00:23:44,892
Na Ji Ni!

432
00:23:52,964 --> 00:23:56,631
After putting me through all this,
they're out at art exhibitions?

433
00:24:28,024 --> 00:24:29,581
Are you really a workaholic?

434
00:24:30,081 --> 00:24:31,916
Do you realize you've been talking
about paintings the whole meal?

435
00:24:32,691 --> 00:24:35,301
How can I just ignore a great painting
when I see one?

436
00:24:35,622 --> 00:24:39,598
I told you, Professor Bae's paintings look
different from different angles.

437
00:24:42,578 --> 00:24:45,192
Couldn't we do the same
with our picture book?

438
00:24:46,005 --> 00:24:48,048
You mean printing it
with a lenticular effect?

439
00:24:48,302 --> 00:24:49,302
Yeah.

440
00:24:50,551 --> 00:24:52,095
Would it be cost-effective?

441
00:24:52,776 --> 00:24:53,776
We'll have to try it.

442
00:24:56,471 --> 00:24:59,638
I love talking about things like this
with you, Ji Ni.

443
00:25:00,126 --> 00:25:01,364
And I enjoyed the exhibition.

444
00:25:03,685 --> 00:25:05,046
Actually,

445
00:25:05,887 --> 00:25:08,584
a lot has been making me
angry and frustrated lately.

446
00:25:09,132 --> 00:25:10,565
But I had a good evening.

447
00:25:11,072 --> 00:25:14,608
Thanks to you,
I was able to forget about all that.

448
00:25:15,296 --> 00:25:16,488
Thank you.

449
00:25:17,477 --> 00:25:18,565
Thank you too.

450
00:25:22,692 --> 00:25:24,357
When I'm with you, I...

451
00:25:28,633 --> 00:25:29,633
I...

452
00:25:30,485 --> 00:25:31,823
feel alive.

453
00:25:35,205 --> 00:25:37,391
There were so many times I wanted to die,

454
00:25:39,307 --> 00:25:40,531
but you make me want to live.

455
00:25:45,205 --> 00:25:46,281
Ji Hu.

456
00:25:48,892 --> 00:25:50,173
The person...

457
00:25:51,145 --> 00:25:52,835
who brings out my honest self.

458
00:25:54,545 --> 00:25:56,125
The person who keeps me alive.

459
00:25:57,585 --> 00:25:58,707
So the person...

460
00:25:59,887 --> 00:26:01,545
I can't help but love.

461
00:26:06,445 --> 00:26:07,515
It's you, Ji Ni.

462
00:26:11,478 --> 00:26:13,103
Ever since we got out
of that storage room...

463
00:26:13,104 --> 00:26:14,177
Please stop.

464
00:26:15,691 --> 00:26:16,861
This is getting so old.

465
00:26:17,100 --> 00:26:18,691
Why is everyone acting like this...

466
00:26:19,758 --> 00:26:21,085
everywhere I go, morning and night?

467
00:26:22,445 --> 00:26:24,270
Do you have nothing else to talk about
besides love?

468
00:26:25,325 --> 00:26:29,098
Will something go wrong
if I don't fall in love in my 20s?

469
00:26:30,184 --> 00:26:32,352
- Ji Ni.
- I hate love.

470
00:26:32,720 --> 00:26:33,996
I don't want it.

471
00:26:34,171 --> 00:26:35,837
How many times do I have to say it?

472
00:26:36,145 --> 00:26:37,779
Do you think I'm just saying this?

473
00:26:38,472 --> 00:26:40,591
You saw what I was like
in that storage room.

474
00:26:41,391 --> 00:26:43,417
You saw how much I loved my dad.

475
00:26:44,592 --> 00:26:47,123
But the lesson my dad taught me was...

476
00:26:47,714 --> 00:26:49,343
"Don't fall in love."

477
00:26:50,472 --> 00:26:52,157
I really hate how intense love can be...

478
00:26:52,393 --> 00:26:55,645
when it makes you lose who you are.

479
00:26:55,992 --> 00:26:57,087
Why are you getting mad?

480
00:26:58,265 --> 00:27:00,718
- Why do you shut everyone out?
- Because I hate it.

481
00:27:01,051 --> 00:27:03,454
Because I've seen my parents
and I know how terrifying love can be!

482
00:27:05,415 --> 00:27:06,415
Do Hee!

483
00:27:07,018 --> 00:27:08,711
Who are you to get mad at Ji Hu?

484
00:27:09,612 --> 00:27:12,080
Why are you clinging to a woman like this?

485
00:27:12,578 --> 00:27:14,017
See? You did leave me for her.

486
00:27:16,249 --> 00:27:17,249
Why?

487
00:27:17,725 --> 00:27:18,725
Does that bother you?

488
00:27:19,545 --> 00:27:20,664
Just stop it!

489
00:27:27,724 --> 00:27:30,658
- Na Ji Ni!
- I told you not to let this happen!

490
00:27:31,313 --> 00:27:32,703
I told you I didn't want this!

491
00:28:00,448 --> 00:28:03,695
(Family Register)

492
00:28:03,697 --> 00:28:06,490
Don't you ever touch Ji Ni again.
I won't let it slide.

493
00:28:06,531 --> 00:28:08,766
Ji Hu confessed to you, right?

494
00:28:08,768 --> 00:28:09,851
It was Ji Ni again.

495
00:28:09,852 --> 00:28:11,279
Who's the woman you met at the hotel?

496
00:28:11,280 --> 00:28:13,067
Is Sa Bin's brother Im Joong Bin?

497
00:28:13,069 --> 00:28:14,317
It wasn't you, right?

498
00:28:14,318 --> 00:28:17,470
I'm going to die.
Because I'm lonely. Because I'm sad.

499
00:28:17,472 --> 00:28:19,978
I've chosen Ji Ni.
There is no second choice.

500
00:28:19,979 --> 00:28:22,886
You'll regret falling in love
with Na Ji Ni more than anything.

501
00:28:24,662 --> 00:28:26,662
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
